1
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:13,000
This is 2147 News Network, broadcasting from the New Delhi Orbital Broadcast Hub. Tonight, Mars enters its final voting cycle.

2
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:43,000
Good evening. I’m Anaya Rao at the Earth-Orbit Media Ring. Across forty-two Martian settlement zones, voters are entering the final hours of a sovereignty referendum that could create the first independent off-world republic in human history.

3
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:35,000
Tonight’s top stories: Mars votes on independence. Earth Union officials prepare an emergency legal review. Helion Grid Systems warns of energy-contract uncertainty. Lunar workers connect oxygen-credit demands to the Mars autonomy debate.

4
00:01:45,000 --> 00:02:50,000
The Mars Civic Council Election Board reports projected turnout at ninety-one percent, with twenty-nine point four million eligible voters. The current settlement model shows fifty-seven percent supporting independence, thirty-nine percent supporting continued union administration, and four percent still undecided.

5
00:03:02,000 --> 00:03:56,000
This vote did not appear suddenly. In 2136, lunar oxygen-credit protests turned life-support pricing into a political rights issue. In 2142, Mars challenged Earth Union cargo tariff authority.

6
00:04:04,000 --> 00:04:30,000
Dr. Ilyan Sen, political historian at the University of Valles Marineris, told 2147 News Network: Mars is no longer an outpost. It is a civilization asking for political recognition.

7
00:04:38,000 --> 00:05:23,000
The political uncertainty is already moving through the economy. Helion Grid Systems CEO Jiang Lau warned that unresolved Earth-Mars treaty language could delay long-term fusion-grid contracts.

8
00:05:30,000 --> 00:06:13,000
The Synthetic Rights Tribunal has received a petition asking whether registered memory-continuity residents in Martian settlement zones can be included in referendum certification.

9
00:06:21,000 --> 00:06:35,000
For Earth, Luna, Mars, and the Outer Belt, this is 2147 News Network. End transmission.
